================================================================================
  SENTRY INCIDENT ANALYZER — API ENDPOINT USAGE GUIDE
  Base URL: http://localhost:8000
================================================================================

All requests require the appropriate Content-Type header.
Authenticated endpoints require: Authorization: Bearer <session-token>


================================================================================
1. ROOT & HEALTH
================================================================================

### 1.1 — Root (service info)
GET /

### 1.2 — Health Check
GET /api/health


================================================================================
2. AUTHENTICATION & USERS
================================================================================

### 2.1 — Login
POST /api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "password",
  "ipaddress": "192.168.1.100",
  "user_agent": "Mozilla/5.0"
}

Note: ipaddress and user_agent are optional — they auto-detect from the
request if omitted.


### 2.2 — Register / Create a New User
POST /api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "username": "johndoe",
  "password": "securepassword123",
  "role": "user"
}


### 2.3 — List All Roles
GET /api/roles


================================================================================
3. AGENT MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

### 3.1 — List All Agents
GET /api/agents


### 3.2 — Add a New Agent (via unified POST)
POST /api/agents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "add",
  "name": "log_classifier_agent",
  "llm_model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5",
  "temperature": 0.2,
  "conn_url": "https://api.anthropic.com",
  "api_key": "skprj-xxxxxxxx",
  "is_primary": false,
  "is_active": true
}

Note: "action" can be omitted — defaults to "add" when no agent_id is present.


### 3.3 — Update an Agent (via unified POST)
POST /api/agents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "update",
  "agent_id": 1,
  "name": "log_classifier_agent_v2",
  "llm_model": "openai/gpt-4o",
  "temperature": 0.2,
  "conn_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
  "api_key": "skprj-yyyyyyyy",
  "is_primary": true,
  "is_active": true
}

Note: If "action" is omitted but agent_id IS provided, it defaults to "update".


### 3.4 — Delete an Agent (via unified POST)
POST /api/agents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "delete",
  "agent_id": 1,
  "name": "log_classifier_agent"
}


### 3.5 — Update an Agent (RESTful PUT)
PUT /api/agents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent_id": 1,
  "name": "log_classifier_agent_v2",
  "llm_model": "openai/gpt-4o",
  "temperature": 0.2,
  "conn_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
  "api_key": "skprj-yyyyyyyy",
  "is_primary": true,
  "is_active": false
}

Or with agent_id in the path:
PUT /api/agents/1


### 3.6 — Delete an Agent (RESTful DELETE)
DELETE /api/agents/1

Or with a JSON body:
DELETE /api/agents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent_id": 1,
  "name": "log_classifier_agent"
}


================================================================================
4. LLM CONFIGURATION
================================================================================

### 4.1 — Get Current LLM Config
GET /api/llm

Returns the active primary model name and temperature.


### 4.2 — Update LLM Config
PUT /api/llm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "openai/gpt-4o",
  "temperature": 0.2
}

Also accepts POST:
POST /api/llm

Note: At least one of "model" or "temperature" must be provided.


================================================================================
5. LOG ANALYSIS
================================================================================

### 5.1 — Analyze Logs (JSON payload)
POST /api/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "logs": "2026-05-10T10:23:45Z ERROR OOM killed process\n2026-05-10T10:24:12Z WARN High memory usage",
  "description": "Kubernetes cluster logs",
  "model_name": "openai/gpt-4o",
  "user": "admin"
}


### 5.2 — Analyze Logs (File Upload)
POST /api/analyze
Content-Type: multipart/form-data

Form field "file": <attach .log, .txt, .json, or .csv file>

Alternatively, send raw text via a form field:
Form field "logs": "<raw log text>"


### 5.3 — Analyze Logs (control response format)
POST /api/analyze?response_format=json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "logs": "ERROR: disk full on /dev/sda1"
}

response_format options:
  "text"  — (default) returns plain-text formatted output
  "json"  — returns structured JSON with classified_entries, remediations, etc.


================================================================================
6. ANALYSIS HISTORY
================================================================================

### 6.1 — Get All Analysis History
GET /api/history


### 6.2 — Filter History by Status
GET /api/history?status=completed
GET /api/history?p_status=failed


### 6.3 — Filter History by Model
GET /api/history?model_name=openai/gpt-4o
GET /api/history?p_model_name=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5


### 6.4 — Filter History by Analysis Code
GET /api/history?analysis_code=ANL-1234567890


### 6.5 — Full-Text Search in History
GET /api/history?content_query=OOM
GET /api/history?p_content_query=disk+full


### 6.6 — Combine Multiple Filters
GET /api/history?status=completed&model_name=openai/gpt-4o&content_query=OOM


### 6.7 — Get Full Details for an Analysis
GET /api/history?analysis_code=ANL-1234567890&include_details=true

Or use the shorthand path:
GET /api/history/ANL-1234567890

Returns: input_text, error_message, classified_entries, remediations


================================================================================
7. API DOCUMENTATION (AUTO-GENERATED)
================================================================================

### 7.1 — Swagger UI (Interactive)
GET /docs

### 7.2 — ReDoc (Read-only)
GET /redoc


